    "narrative": "The Zurich Zebras enter today\u2019s slate with **Pete Crow-Armstrong** (73.77) and **Yordan Alvarez** (72.97) leading the charge as our top-tier plays. **Pete Crow-Armstrong** is a mandatory start; his elite speed profile combined with an aggressive matchup against Gausman\u2014who allows a high volume of stolen base opportunities\u2014makes him our most valuable catalyst. Meanwhile, **Yordan Alvarez** remains the heart of our production, benefiting from an elite xwOBA and a favorable matchup against Bibee. **Junior Caminero** (67.50) also earns a high-confidence start, capitalizing on the high xERA of Poulin. We are leaning heavily into the platoon edges offered by **Lars Nootbaar** (61.48), whose matchup against Lugo provides a necessary boost to our mid-range production, helping to offset the risks associated with the leaner bottom-of-the-order slots.\n\nThe decision to bench our remaining depth was largely dictated by the restrictive nature of our game cap management. While **Christian Yelich** (59.62) posted the highest mark among our non-starters, his platoon disadvantage against P\u00e9rez and the scarcity of high-upside spots kept him on the pine. **Dillon Dingler** (57.51) was the most difficult exclusion, narrowly edged out by our positional requirements; his wind-aided park factor and favorable matchup against Eisert were enticing, but the necessity of maintaining roster flexibility in the MI and utility spots favored our current configuration. We are closely monitoring weather reports regarding wind patterns for the games involving **Chase Meidroth** and **Colt Keith**, as their scores are particularly sensitive to atmospheric shifts; should the wind die down, those marginal scores could drop below the viability floor. We remain thin in the infield due to **Hyeseong Kim** and **Rece Hinds** being currently stashed in the minors, leaving us limited internal cover should any of today's starters face an unexpected late-scratch.",
